  "sgg_form_id": null,
  "description": "SF424 Mandatory Form (SF424_Mandatory_3_0) is a streamlined variant of the SF-424 used for formula grants, block grants, and other mandatory awards. Unlike the standard SF-424, it includes submission type, frequency, version, and consolidated request fields, but has a reduced estimated funding section (Federal and Match only, versus 7 line items on the standard SF-424).",
  "notes": [
    "Uses the SF-424 family's shared sections (opportunity, application, applicant, project, contacts, budget, certification, and attachments), built from question bank questions. The point of contact and authorized representative are separate answers under contacts, and neither asks for an address.",
    "The agency and assistance listing fields are under opportunity, with assistance_listing nested inside it, as in the rest of the family.",
    "The DAT requires the applicant organization, its EIN, and its address, but the XSD lets the applicant leave out Organization entirely. The form follows the DAT, and the XML structure doesn't change.",
    "Six fields are required only when their question calls for them: other submission type, other frequency, the consolidated request explanation, other applicant type, the state review date, and the delinquent debt explanation.",
    "SGG fills in the received date, signature, and signature date when the application is submitted, so they're optional in a draft. The agency, assistance listing, and UEI are read-only and pre-populated by the API.",
    "Department and division reuse the bank questions with the XSD's 30-character limit. The project title (250 characters), areas affected (250 characters), and funding period dates are local to the form: the bank's project title allows 200 characters, and the funding period is the period the funds cover, not the project's start and end.",
    "Supporting documents are an optional list of up to 100 uploaded files. The additional congressional districts attachment is a single file.",
    "Estimated funding reuses the bank's budget amount: a string of up to 12 digits with optional cents, so no amount is rounded. The XML mapping writes it with two decimal places.",
    "The layout asks for the applicant type with the applicant organization and asks for the received dates together. The XML order doesn't change."
  ],
  "risks": [
    "Changing Country can leave both State and Province in an answer. The XSD allows only one, so that answer fails XSD validation. The fix belongs in the shared address question, for every form that uses it.",
    "The attachment IDs in the preview's sample data aren't real uploaded files.",
    "The state review choices show the XSD's codes (StateReviewAvailable, StateReviewNotSelected, and StateReviewNotNeeded) in the preview. The install PR adds the DAT's wording as display labels in SGG.",
    "The DAT's burden statement cites OMB 4040-0002, but the form information and the PDF header say 4040-0020. The form uses 4040-0020."
  ],
